{
  "name": "MTR-101",
  "description": "P-101 drive. Running feedback is discrete input 10003, ready 10004, trip 10005. Start is coil 1 and the field reset is coil 3. The trip is inverted into the interlock, because DEVCTL's INTERLOCK is a *permit* — True means may run — and wiring a trip straight to it would let the motor run only while it was tripped. The start permissive is the drive being ready AND a speed reference above 5 %: the plant starts the motor from the VFD, so a start with the drive at rest can never get its run feedback and would sit in Starting until the 10 s timer faulted it. Refusing it up front is what the operator can act on.",
